# PS2-G21-2 option B (NOT preferred, sketch): check the shrinking reallocations and fail. A shrink that fails leaves a perfectly usable larger array, so failing is both unnecessary and expensive: the failure happens between collectives and would need its own agreement (the edge-array one could ride the final reduction, the multinode one cannot), and the realloc'ed-to-NULL array is leaked. Option A keeps the array, as the maintainer's tree already does for the send index array of dgraphGhst2() after G19.
# (applies to the combined series base, i.e. v7.0.17 + the 20 finished groups)
diff --git a/src/libscotch/dgraph_coarsen.c b/src/libscotch/dgraph_coarsen.c
index 09540aa..b035a44 100644
--- a/src/libscotch/dgraph_coarsen.c
+++ b/src/libscotch/dgraph_coarsen.c
